values
(
  'afterglow', 'Afterglow', 'Blakesville Creamery',
  'Port Washington', 'Wisconsin', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Goat', 'Animal', 'Washed-rind, smear-ripened, uncooked/unpressed, modeled after Langres',
  '60 days', array['lactic', 'yeasty', 'tangy', 'malty', 'fruity'],
  'Washed in cherry ale and aged to a dense, fudgy texture, Afterglow is a washed-rind goat cheese that brings quiet funk and real character. The beer adds subtle fruit and lift, rounding out the savory depth of Blakesville’s pasture-raised milk. This is the cheese you reach for when you want something bold, but not brash, something that plays well with prosciutto, rye crisps, or tart fruit preserves. It’s structured, aromatic, and always the most talked-about square on the board. Blakesville is known for thoughtful, small-batch cheeses made entirely on their farm using their own Alpine herd. From pasture to cave, everything happens on site, allowing for a level of detail that’s rare, and it shows.', array['Cherry ale', 'cherry juice', 'rose bubbles', 'cherry liqueur', 'cherry cola', 'cherries!'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'barista', 'Barista', 'Kaasboerderij’t Groendal',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Roeselare', 'Belgium',
  'Pasteurized cow', 'Animal', 'Washed rind/Treated Rind',
  '18 months', array['Smooth', 'buttery', 'coffee'],
  'Kaasboerderij ''t Groendal is a cheese producer located in Belgium, specifically in the region of West Flanders. The dairy farm focuses on producing artisanal cheeses using milk from their own herd of cows. Their product range includes several types of Gouda, including unique varieties infused with herbs and other flavors. The farm is operated by the family Desmet. This cheese starts as an Abbey-style, washed rind cheese that gets treated with coffee grounds and possesses a layer of coffee grounds in the center.', array['Drinking chocolate', 'cinnamon tea', 'White Russian', 'Effie’s biscuits'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'cabricafe', 'Cabricafe', 'La Fermier de Mean',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Ardenne', 'Belgium',
  'Raw Goat’s milk', 'traditional', 'semi-soft, washed rind',
  'unknown', array['Roast Coffee', 'Heavy Cream', 'Sourdough', 'Yeast'],
  'This raw goat cheese is washed with crushed coffee beans. It has semi-soft texture that is sometimes custardy soft and sometimes a touch more firm with a full flavor that''s fruity, meaty yeasty. It is a very unique cheese', array['coffee with milk', 'shortbread cookies'],
