(
  'langres-pronounced-long-wruh', 'Langres (pronounced long-wruh)', 'Fromagerie Germain',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Champagne-Ardenne region in', 'France',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal', 'Washed-Rind, Smear-ripened, Uncooked/unpressed',
  'Minimum 21 days', array['Doughy', 'pungent', 'lactic', 'tangy', 'buttermilky'],
  'Langres was declared CDO (Certified Designation of Origin) in 1991 then PDO (Protected Designation of Origin) in 2012. The Langres AOP Germain is a cheese made from cow’s milk with a soft centre and a washed rind. The cheese is matured according to a ver y demanding method of successive washings which gives it a beautiful orange colour. It''s a cheese that has a pungent, intense and characteristic aroma which gives way to a fairly mild taste. The Langres AOP Germain is the leading Langres cheese in the world.', array['Puligny-Montrachet', 'autolytic bubbles', 'Gose', 'apple juice', 'apples', 'grapes', 'sourdough bread', 'saussicon sec', 'traditionally paired with bubbles into the concave part', 'but most of us agree that it makes the cheese slimy and gross–best have the bubbles on the side'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'le-bruzy', 'Le Bruzy', 'La Fermière de Mean',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Southeast', 'Belgium',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Washed Rind/Trappist',
  '4-5 weeks', array['Tart', 'pungent', 'buttermilk', 'meaty', 'springy textured'],
  'La Fermière de Mean is a cooperative dairy farm located in southeastern Belgium, founded in 1986. The farm aims to raise animals in a humane manner and operate their farms in an environmentally sound way. They produce a variety of cheeses, including Cabricharme. Le Bruzy is a Trappist style cheese, made in the traditional style that is tried and true.', array['Trappist ale', 'apples', 'pears', 'cured meat', 'crusty bread', 'dry cider'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'mild-brick', 'Mild Brick', 'Widmer’s Cheese Cellars',
  'Theresa', 'WI', 'USA',
  'pasteurized, cow’s milk', 'traditional', 'american original, washed rind',
  '1-3 months', array['Tangy', 'Savory', 'Roasted Nuts'],
  'this cheese is totally unique and an american original. Brick cheese gets its name from the bricks used to weigh down blocks of this iconic Wisconsin original when it was first developed by Swiss immigrant John Jossi in 1877. Widmers has been producing cheese since 1922. They still use bricks in their production', array['hot honey', 'peanuts', 'apple soda', 'sweet vermouth', 'grilled cheese', 'tomato soup. Traditionally for Detroit style pizza'],
