(
  'nabbabo', 'Nabbabo', 'CasArrigoni',
  'Valtaleggio', 'Lombardy', 'Italy',
  'Pasteurized Goat', 'Animal', 'Washed Rind',
  '40 days', array['Pungent', 'tart', 'buttermilky', 'rich', 'meltable', 'funky'],
  'A washed-rind cheese that is slightly pink in color. On the inside, the paste is the bright white characteristic of soft goat cheese. Nababbo has a creamy and supple texture that closely resembles typical Lombard cheeses. It is aged in our cellars for over 40 days. The result has a mild, buttery and rich flavor that retains the distinctive aftertaste of goat’s milk with a hint of bitterness, also typical of goat cheese. Coming from the same place where Taleggio is made, this cheese is made in the same style, but with goat’s milk.', array['Valtellina', 'malty beer', 'Pinot Grigio', 'cured meats'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'oma', 'Oma', 'Von Trapp Farmstead',
  'Waitsfield', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized, organic cow’s milk', 'Animal', 'Smear-ripened, washed-rind, uncooked/unpressed',
  '60-90 days', array['Beefy', 'earthy', 'buttery', 'rich', 'pungent'],
  'Our family has run the von Trapp Farmstead since 1959, when Werner and Erika von Trapp moved to Waitsfield, Vermont to grow crops and raise livestock, and to build a sustainable future for their children. Today, we make award winning cheese, organic yogurt, and pastured meat from our regeneratively raised cows and pigs. We believe that wholesome, flavorful food begins with healthy soil and animals. Our products are infused with a deep appreciation & desire to honor the land and cows that allow us to practice our craft. Sebastian von Trapp grew up on the family farm, with his Opa and Oma (Werner and Erika) living just down the road. His parents, Martin and Kelly, ran the farm and dairy, selling their milk to local buyers at whatever price was set by the whims of the global dairy market. In 2007, he began construction on a creamery for making cheese out of the farm’s milk, with the goal of creating more sustainable income for the farm. The von Trapp Farmstead started making cheese in 2009. Molly Semler grew up in Middlesex, Vermont and returned to the state to follow her passion for making cheese. She started working on the farm over a decade ago, and over the course of making cheese together, she and Sebastian fell in love. (Cheesy, but true!) Sebastian currently runs the farm while Molly operates the creamery.', array['Earthy', 'herbaceous red wines', 'funky ale', 'sidra', 'cherry cola', 'birch beer', 'smokey scotch', 'gherkins', 'salami'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'opa', 'Opa', 'Von Trapp Farmstead',
  'Waitsfield', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal', 'Smear-ripened, washed rind, uncooked/unpressed',
  '60-90 days', array['Beefy', 'earthy', 'buttery', 'rich', 'pungent'],
  'Our family has run the von Trapp Farmstead since 1959, when Werner and Erika von Trapp moved to Waitsfield, Vermont to grow crops and raise livestock, and to build a sustainable future for their children. Today, we make award winning cheese, organic yogurt, and pastured meat from our regeneratively raised cows and pigs. We believe that wholesome, flavorful food begins with healthy soil and animals. Our products are infused with a deep appreciation & desire to honor the land and cows that allow us to practice our craft. Sebastian von Trapp grew up on the family farm, with his Opa and Oma (Werner and Erika) living just down the road. His parents, Martin and Kelly, ran the farm and dairy, selling their milk to local buyers at whatever price was set by the whims of the global dairy market. In 2007, he began construction on a creamery for making cheese out of the farm’s milk, with the goal of creating more sustainable income for the farm. The von Trapp Farmstead started making cheese in 2009. Molly Semler grew up in Middlesex, Vermont and returned to the state to follow her passion for making cheese. She started working on the farm over a decade ago, and over the course of making cheese together, she and Sebastian fell in love. (Cheesy, but true!) Sebastian currently runs the farm while Molly operates the creamery.', array['Earthy', 'herbaceous red wines', 'funky ale', 'sidra', 'cherry cola', 'birch beer', 'smokey scotch', 'gherkins', 'salami'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'pawlet', 'Pawlet', 'Woodlawn Creamery',
  'Pawlet', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Washed rind, Italian Toma',
  '3-6 months', array['Mild', 'grassy', 'browned butter', 'raw nuts'],
  'Pawlet is named for the small town in Vermont’s Mettawee Valley where the Leach family has farmed for 7 generations. Chartered in 1761 as part of the New Hampshire Grants, Pawlet expanded after the Revolutionary War, when soldiers who had noted its agricultural promise on their way to halt Burgoyne’s march from Canada returned with their families to farm what the Narragansett called the “valley of black earth.” Pawlet the cheese reflects that rich agricultural history, made with milk from our Registered Holstein herd that is born, fed, pastured, and milked right here at home. The result tastes like our valley—rich, grassy, earthy, and beautiful.', array['Great for cooking–gratins', 'grilled cheese', 'etc. Pecans', 'apples', 'ciders', 'fruity liqueurs', 'pomegranate juice', 'fresh cherries', 'pickles', 'cured meats'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'smorbier', 'Smorbier', 'High Lawn Farm',
  'Lee', 'Massachusetts', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized cow', 'Animal', 'Washed curd, washed rind',
  '2-4 months', array['Bovine', 'spicy', 'smokey', 'meltable'],
  'High Lawn Farm takes particular pride in the care of their cows. Since their grandparents decided, back in the 1920s, to build a dairy farm of only Jersey cows, their passion has been achieving excellence in all regards, from respecting the Jersey heritage and breeding to the quality of milk produced at the farm. Smorbier is a take on the French classic, Morbier, which is a washed rind cow’s milk cheese with a layer of ash in the middle. It was originally made by farmers/cheese producers for themselves with milk that was left over from Comté production. Instead of an ash layer, this cheese has a line of locally sourced peppers that impart a smokey, spicy kick that is balanced by the creamy, rich paste.', array['Acidic white wine with a little residual sugar', 'sweet cider', 'ale', 'cured meat', 'apples', 'potato chips'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'winnimere', 'Winnimere', 'Jasper Hill Farms',
  'Greensboro', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Bark-wrapped washed-rind (smear-ripened), uncooked/unpressed',
  '60 days', array['bacon', 'woodsy', 'dusty', 'peanut shell', 'smoked brisket', 'savory custard'],
  'WINNIMERE is a take on Jura Mountain classics like Vacherin Mont d’Or or Försterkäse. In keeping with tradition, this decadent cheese is made only during winter months when Jasper Hill’s Ayrshire cows are giving rich, hay-fed raw milk. Winnimere is named for the corner of Caspian Lake where the Kehlers’ grandfather had an ice fishing shack. Young cheeses are wrapped in strips of spruce cambium, the tree’s flexible inner bark layer, harvested from Jasper Hill Farm’s woodlands. During aging, the cheese is washed in a cultured salt brine to help even rind development. At 60 days, this cheese is spoonably soft and tastes of bacon, sweet cream, and spruce.', array['fresh', 'crusty bread', 'roasted brussels sprouts', 'fried potatoes', 'crudite', 'old world Pinot Noir', 'Rioja', 'bubbles', 'herbal tea'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'appalachian', 'Appalachian', 'Meadow Creek Dairy',
  'Galax', 'VA', 'USA',
  'raw, cow’s milk', 'traditional', 'tomme',
  '4-5 months', array['Earthy', 'Velvety', 'Fresh', 'white mushrooms'],
  'From Meadow Creek Dairy, Appalachian is in a cheese in the style of tomme de savoie. Meadow Creek is a farm and dairy focused on great genetics, they’ve been refining their herd since 1988. They also only graze on grass and don’t pasteurize any of their milk. Cheese is only made from mid-March through November. Meadow Creek is owned by the Feete Family; it is in the mountains of southwest Virginia. At an elevation of 2,800 feet, the clean water, clean air, and deep soils produce an ideal environment for growing diverse, rich pastures. This cheese requires some salesmanship so make sure to emphasize how cool the creamery is !', array['Pinot gris', 'ramatos', 'lagers'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'drunken-goat', 'Drunken Goat', 'Mitica (the import arm of Forever Cheese)',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Jumilla', 'Spain',
  'Pasteurized Goat’s Milk', 'Traditional', 'tomme',
  '60 days', array['Red Wine', 'Lactic', 'Sweet Cream'],
  'This is a name branded version of D.O.P Queso de Murcia al Vino. It is a semi-firm goat cheese soaked in the traditional style wine of the region, Doble Pasta, which is made from Monastrell grapes. This is a very starter-friendly cheese for new customers / a good option for people who “don’t like goat cheese”', array['orange blossom honey', 'medium-bodied Spanish reds', 'full bodied white wines', 'chorizo', 'gin based cocktails'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'goliath', 'Goliath', 'McGrath Cheese Company',
  'Hudson Valley', 'NY', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized cow', 'animal', 'farmhouse cheddar, washed rind',
  '3-5 months', array['Sharp', 'grassy', 'savory', 'with a firm', 'slightly dry texture and a subtle nutty', 'lightly fruity finish'],
  'Goliath comes from McGrath Cheese Company in New York’s Hudson Valley. It’s a cheddar-style cheese that’s been rind-washed as it ages, giving it a more savory, slightly “farmy” edge without going funky. It stays clean and approachable, just with a little more personality than your standard cheddar', array['Apple', 'pears', 'mustard', 'mini toasts'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'the-gray', 'The Gray', 'Mystic Cheese',
  'Groton', 'CT', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Ayrshire cow', 'animal rennet', 'UK Red Cheshire, natural rind',
  '90 days', array['Buttery and savory with a bright', 'mouthwatering acidity. Notes of warm butter', 'buttermilk', 'and light minerality', 'with a slightly salty edge and a lingering butterscotch-like finish.'],
  'This is Mystic’s take on a traditional Cheshire, made with milk from Ayrshire cows. They follow the classic method, milling the curds, salting by hand, and pressing slowly to get that crumbly but still creamy texture. It’s made right near the Connecticut coast, which gives it a subtle mineral edge. The orange color comes from annatto, a natural plant-based dye traditionally used in Cheshire and other British-style cheeses.', array['chutney', 'mustard', 'pickles', 'potato chips'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'la-dama-sagrada', 'La Dama Sagrada', 'Mitica imported - Fatima is the name of the cheesemaker',
  'El Carpio de Tajo', 'Toledo', 'Spain',
  'raw, goat’s milk', 'traditional', 'tomme, manchego-style',
  'minimum 6 months', array['Salty', 'Caramel', 'Grassy'],
  'The “Sacred Lady” cheese! Women have been central to European cheesemaking for hundreds of years, but it is still rare to see a woman promoted to head cheesemaker in many European dairies. Fátima Navarro grew up in the cheese world and has over 24 years of experience in the industry. Her family helped found a dairy co-op in El Carpio de Tajo, which produces high quality Murcian goat’s milk. Fátima now serves as master cheesemaker of the co-op with Dama Sagrada as her piece de resistance. La Dama Sagrada is a manchego-style cheese, but made with goat’s milk', array['Tempranillo', 'dry perry', 'sherry', 'olive oil'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'manchego-semi-curado', 'Manchego Semi-Curado', 'Dehesa de los Llanos',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Albacete', 'Spain',
  'raw, sheep’s milk', 'traditional', 'tomme, PDO Manchego',
  'minimum 3 months', array['Greek Yogurt', 'Cashews', 'Tangy'],
  'a classic Manchego cheese. This is a farmstead manchego made on a 10,000 hectare farm property that also produces olive oil. They brush the rind in olive oil giving it a distinct natural-rind, but without too much natural flora.', array['classic pairing is quince paste', 'or membrillo. Verdejo', 'Chardonnay', 'Riojas. Marcona almonds', 'jamon serrano'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'riley-s-2x4', 'Riley’s 2x4', 'Blue Ledge Farm',
  'Salisbury', 'VT', 'USA',
  'Raw goat & cow', 'animal rennet', 'mixed milk, natural rind, cave aged',
  '3 months', array['Nutty and savory with a briny edge', 'balanced by a bright lactic tang. Notes of toasted bread and subtle grassiness', 'with a light', 'lingering sweetness on the finish.'],
  'A true mixed milk cheese made from Blue Ledge Farm’s own goat’s milk and Ayrshire cow’s milk from nearby Mose Farm. Handcrafted and cave aged, allowing a natural rind to develop over time. The name “2x4” refers to the number of teats. Two from goats, four from cows. A staff favorite that balances brightness from the goat’s milk with the richness of cow’s milk.', array['spicy salami', 'cherry', 'Riesling', 'olives'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'tomarashi', 'TomaRashi', 'Point Reyes Farmstead Cheese Co',
  'Point Reyes', 'CA', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized cow', 'Microbial / vegetarian', 'tomme style / flavor added',
  '6–8 weeks', array['damp cellar', 'mushrooms', 'gentle earth', 'citrus lift'],
  'Tomme de Crayeuse is a relatively modern cheese, created in the 1990s by affineur Max Schmidhauser in the Savoie region of France. It was designed as a softer, more expressive alternative to traditional Tomme de Savoie. The name Crayeuse translates to chalky, referencing the distinctive texture at the center of the cheese when young. As it matures, the paste transitions from chalky to supple, while the natural rind develops a gray brown, suede like surface. The flavor profile remains gentle and earthy throughout aging, with notes of damp cellar and mushrooms lifted by a subtle lemony brightness that keeps the cheese fresh and approachable. Customer Type: Tomme lovers, mushroom forward palates, fans of rustic French cheeses. How to sell it in one sentence: “A gentle, earthy tomme with a chalky center, mushroom notes, and a clean lemony finish.”', array['Pinot Noir', 'light Rhône reds', 'crusty bread', 'cornichons'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'wilde-goat', 'Wilde Goat', 'High Lawn Farm',
  'Lee', 'MA', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Jersey cow & Nubian goat', 'animal rennet', 'Alpine, washed rind',
  '4-10 months', array['Nutty and pleasantly sharp with a rich', 'buttery base. Notes of toasted coffee', 'hay', 'and hops with a subtle earthy sweetness from the goat’s milk. Bright upfront with a long', 'slightly fudgy finish.'],
  'A blend of High Lawn’s Jersey cow’s milk and Nubian goat’s milk, Wilde Goat brings together richness and brightness in one wheel. Washed in hazy IPA from a nearby brewery, it picks up subtle hoppy and toasty notes while aging. The texture lands somewhere between alpine and aged cheddar, with a dense, slightly sticky feel that makes it hard to stop at one bite. Seasonal release, so it doesn’t stick around long.', array['roasted potatoes', 'hazy IPA', 'rosemary pesto', 'caramel'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'adiron-jack', 'Adiron-Jack', 'Nettle Meadow',
  'Warrensburg', 'NY', 'USA',
  'pasteurized cow’s milk', 'vegetarian, microbial', 'infused soft ripened',
  'about a month', array['Sour Cream', 'White Mushrooms', 'McIntosh Apples'],
  'Nettle Meadow infuses Adiron-jack with a hint of New York State applejack brandy. Adiron-Jack is a triple-cream made with Jersey cow’s milk. It is not particularly boozy. Nettle Meadow is a sanctuary farm that rehomes retired farm animals in Upstate NY. It is also women owned', array['A brut champagne', 'light riesling', 'farmhouse ale or a hard apple cider accompanied by a lightly salted cracker', 'apple butter', 'prosciutto or thinly-sliced fennel.'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'bonde-d-antan', 'Bonde d’Antan', 'Poitou Chevre',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Poitou-Charentes region of', 'France',
  'pasteurized goat''s milk', 'animal', 'soft',
  '2-6 weeks', array['bright', 'nutty', 'sweet with a tangy lemon finish'],
  'A crottin-style goat cheese from the the Poitou-Charentes/Loire Valley. It has earned silver and bronze awards at the prestigious Concours General Agricole in Paris', array['light honey', 'fig jam', 'baked over a baguette', 'fruity rose wine'],
