(
  'brie-fermier', 'Brie Fermier', 'Tremblaye',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Seine-et-Marne in Ile-de', 'France',
  'Pasteurized, organic cow’s milk', 'Animal', 'Soft-ripened/Bloomy rind',
  '4-5 weeks', array['Buttery', 'creamy', 'mild mushroom', 'fresh and milky'],
  'A traditional farmstead brie made with organic cow’s milk, Tremblaye Organic Brie Fermier is soft-ripened and delicately earthy. Crafted in Île-de-France, it offers a creamy, buttery paste beneath a bloomy white rind, with subtle mushroom notes and a clean, milky finish that reflects its high-quality, organic origins.', array['Fresh fruit', 'champagne', 'hazelnuts', 'crusty bread'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'brie-paysan', 'Brie Paysan', 'Fromagerie du Presbytère',
  'Sainte-Élizabeth-de-Warwick', 'Quebec', 'Canada',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'microbial', 'bloomy rind/brie',
  '~30 days', array['Rich and creamy with warm milk', 'cultured butter', 'cooked mushrooms', 'and soft vegetal notes. The texture is plush and melting', 'with a velvety paste that becomes more luscious as it warms.'],
  'Made by Fromagerie du Presbytère in Quebec, Brie Paysan is a farmstead bloomy rind cheese crafted from the creamery’s own Holstein and Jersey herd. Aged around 30 days, it develops a fluffy white rind and an ultra-creamy interior with deep dairy richness and earthy mushroom character. The name “Paysan,” meaning “farmer” or “country-style,” is a nod to the people who work the land and care for the herd behind the cheese.', array['apricot', 'honey', 'paler chardonnay', 'champagne'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'camembert-reo', 'Camembert Reo', 'Fromagerie Réo',
  'Lessay', 'Normandy', 'France',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal', 'soft ripened/Bloomy rind',
  'min. 21 days', array['Rich and velvety with notes of cultured butter', 'cooked mushrooms', 'garlic', 'hay', 'and warm cream. The paste becomes soft and marshmallowy as it ripens', 'developing a savory', 'brothy depth with a clean earthy finish.'],
  'Made in Lessay, Normandy by Fromagerie Réo, this traditional Camembert has been hand-ladled since 1931 using milk sourced from nearby farms within a 30 km radius of the dairy. The authentic French version carries AOP/PDO protection and is made from raw milk, while the US-imported version is gently pasteurized to meet regulations without losing its traditional character. Réo remains one of the few larger producers still committed to careful hand-ladling and classic Normandy cheesemaking methods.', array['chocolate', 'apple', 'mushroom pate', 'bake it!'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'ca-a-de-cabra', 'Caña de Cabra', 'Central Quesera Montesinos',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Murcia', 'Spain',
  'Pasteurized Goat', 'Animal', 'Soft-ripened/Bloomy Rind',
  '21 days', array['Clean', 'bright', 'lemony', 'peppery rind'],
  'Murcia is famous for its quality goat’s milk, and Caña de Cabra, a soft-ripened goat log, showcases this milk. The cheese is made by Central Quesera Montesinos, an expert in goat''s milk cheeses with whom Mitica has partnered for many years. Caña de Cabra has a white mold rind and a fudgy interior. Aged 21 days, it becomes firmer as it ages further, with the cream line along the rind becoming more pronounced. As with most Murciana goat''s milk cheeses, the flavor is mild, never goaty. When young, the cheese is mild with a slight tang, gaining intensity and a mushroomy flavor with age.', array['Bubbles', 'acidic whites', 'sparkling water', 'lemonade'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
