),
(
  'robiola-bosina', 'Robiola Bosina', 'Caseificio dell’Alta Langa',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Piedmont', 'Italy',
  'cow and sheep milk', 'animal', 'soft',
  '10-15 days', array['mild', 'buttery', 'earthy', 'mushroom with hints of sweetness and salt'],
  'cheese is named after Bosia, the village where the creamery is located, the steep hilly terrain of the area was historically too rugged for large cattle farming and families had a few cows and a small flock of sheep; during the spring and summer calving seasons the milk production fluctuated and in order to make a batch of cheese local women were forced to pool the available milk blending the cow and sheep milk in the same bucket; they accidentally found that the cow’s milk provide a sweet buttery base and that the sheep’s milk which was high in fat added a velvety richness', array['fresh berries and honey', 'marcona almonds', 'prosciutto', 'warm sourdough bread'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'shabby-shoe', 'Shabby Shoe', 'Blakesville Creamery',
  'Port Washington', 'WI', 'USA',
  'pasteurized goat’s milk', 'microbial', 'bloomy rind, geotrichum base',
  '3 weeks before shipping & up to 90 days', array['Heavy Cream', 'Lemony', 'Tart', 'Earthy Minerality'],
  'based on the French cheese, Chabichou, this is a larger format geotrichum-rinded goat cheese. From Blakeville Creamery, led by Veronica Pedraza, this creamery is located on the same plot of land as the farm, but because it has two separate owners it is not necessarily farmstead in origin', array['best paired with french white wines from the Loire', 'effie’s corn crackers', 'Flouwer Crackers', 'or lemon curd'],
