),
(
  'bella-bantam', 'Bella Bantam', 'Arethusa Farm',
  'Litchfield', 'CT', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized, cow’s milk', 'traditional', 'tomme',
  '1-4 months', array['Buttered Popcorn', 'Salty', 'Fresh Milk'],
  'An aged cow’s milk cheese. Very mild and good for melting. In 1999 Manolo Blahnik execs, and partners, George Malkemus and Anthony Yurgaitis bought the farm in 1999 to “save open farmland”. George passed in 2021, but Anthony continues to fund the farm. Arethusa Farm started in 1868', array['berry jams', 'apricots', 'effies oat cakes', 'Belgian farmhouse ales', 'Chardonnays'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'cravero-parmigiano-reggiano', 'Cravero Parmigiano Reggiano', 'Cheesemaker Massimo Libra Latterie 2659 in Benedello di Pavullo, est. 1973, aged by Cravery, imported by Essex St. Cheese',
  'Benedello di Pavullo', 'aged in Bra', 'Italy',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Grana',
  'Minimum 12 months, but many are aged 24-36 months', array['Softer texture than other parmigiano', 'acidic', 'savory', 'toothsome'],
  'Giorgio Cravero’s family has selected and aged Parmigiano Reggiano in Bra, Italy since 1855. Just off the main drag of the town of Bra, home to Slow Food’s biennial Cheese festival, lie the halls of Cravero. Twenty-foot high rooms that hold five thousand wheels of Parmigiano Reggiano. Cravero’s wheels rest on pine and they turn their wheels more frequently than other agers with an aim to make a softer, less cakey texture. Aging rooms like Cravero’s have long been a part of the cycle of making and selling Parmigiano Reggiano, much like they are for other long-aged cheeses like Comté and Gouda, cheeses whose lengthy affinage represents a real cash flow issue to farmers and cheesemakers.', array['Prosecco', 'robust red wines', 'sprite', 'prosciutto', 'olives', 'snacky fare or in recipes'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'fulvi-pecorino-romano', 'Fulvi Pecorino Romano', 'Fulvi',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Lazio', 'Italy',
  'Raw Sheep', 'Animal', 'Cooked, Pressed',
  '10-12 months', array['Salty', 'briny', 'pastoral', 'lanolin', 'dry', 'crumbly'],
  'Fulvi Pecorino Romano is an authentic Italian cheese made from 100% sheep''s milk, produced in the Roman countryside. It is known for its moon-white interior, feathery granular texture, and a briny, slightly peppery flavor. This cheese is traditionally aged for 10 months to 1 year and is coated in black wax, making it distinct from other Pecorino Romano cheeses. Fulvi Pecorino Romano is celebrated for its rich taste, being less salty and dry compared to other varieties, and is often described as pleasantly gamey with a complex flavor profile.', array['Used for cooking', 'Aglianico', 'Left Bank Bordeaux', 'Sagrantino', 'sweet cider', 'pomegranate juice', 'drinking chocolate'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'ragusano', 'Ragusano', 'Guffanti',
  'Ragusa', 'Sicily', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', '{asta Filata',
  'Minimum 90 days', array['Saline', 'briney', 'springy texture', 'good stretch when melted'],
  'In Sicily, caciocavallo traditionally takes the shape of a parallelepiped. To be Ragusano DOP, it must be produced with milk from Modicana cows, now rare and almost extinct, fed on grass or hay. Otherwise, if the milk comes from cows of other breeds, it takes the name “Cosacavaddu Rausanu”. The pastures they come from are those of the Iblean plateau, poor but characterised by a great variety of spontaneous flora and aromatic herbs. This cheese is stored in pairs on a string to allow the forms to air out as best as possible, and hung from a beam, as is done with round caciocavallo. During the maturing process, the cheeses are greased with oil mixed with vinegar. Due to the size of the cheeses, their production requires great manual skill on the part of the cheesemaker, who uses traditional techniques and tools.', array['Etna DOP', 'saline white wines', 'like Spanish Albariño', 'Muscadet Sevre et Marne', 'iced tea', 'ground mustard', 'whole muscle charcuterie'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'sierra-la-solana', 'Sierra la Solana', 'Sierra la Solana Farm, Cheesemaker Maria Jose Gonzales',
  'La Mancha', 'Spaine', 'Spain',
  'Raw Sheep', 'Animal', 'Manchego, cooked/pressed',
  '6 months', array['Truffly', 'umami', 'clean', 'pastoral'],
  'Using locally foraged Tuber Melanosporum truffles that are harvested in Teruel, Spain by a woman-owned company, Sierra La Salona is a diamond in the rough. These cooked truffles are added to the milk of Manchega breed ewes, all born on Finca Sierra de la Solana Farm founded in La Mancha, Spain in 1878. The curds are then pressed into the traditional Manchego molds of the region, resulting in truffle as a perfect expression of terroir. Cheesemaker Maria José Gonzalez works with 1200 Manchego ewes whose lambs are born in the spring and fall to the quiet playing of Mariachi music, and they feed on a mix of native grains grown on the farm.', array['Cencibel (Tempranillo)', 'Hazy IPA', 'Dr. Pepper', 'Black Tea', 'Jamon', 'Olives'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'brabander', 'Brabander', 'A cooperative Dairy and sold through L’Amuse, imported by Essex',
  'Zigerfeld', 'Holland', 'Netherlands',
  'Pasteurized Saanen Goat', 'Animal', 'Gouda',
  '6-9 months', array['Sweet', 'nutty', 'delicate', 'candied', 'approachable'],
  'Betty Koster founded Fromagerie l’Amuse in 1989 with her husband Martin. Their Amsterdam shop is a destination for cheese lovers, featuring rare, small-production Dutch gems like Wilde Weide and Terschelling. Betty’s deep, long-term connections with Dutch farmers, cheesemakers and opleggers (affineurs) has given her access to an unparalleled range of cheeses. She exports a handful to America exclusively through Essex St. Cheese. Opleggers: Dutch cheese affinage is managed by an oplegger who operates as a milk middle-man, buying cheese when it’s young, selling cheese when it’s older. The word comes from the Dutch verb “to lay something on a shelf,” which is a lovely understatement of the work these craftsmen cheese agers do.Betty''s opleggers sometimes age wheels at warmer-than-normal temperatures. It’s a high wire act of affinage, one that can produce off flavors if not done carefully.', array['Dutch Dubbel and Trippel Ales', 'Argentinian Malbec', 'plush Merlot', 'Ginger beer', 'fresh fruit'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'buffelkaas-buffalo-gouda', 'Buffelkaas (Buffalo Gouda)', 'Treur Kaas',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Woerden', 'Netherlands',
  'pasteurized buffalo milk', 'Vegetarian', 'Gouda style, semi firm',
  '8 weeks', array['Mild', 'creamy', 'and smooth with a soft', 'buttery body. Light sweetness from the buffalo milk with subtle notes of fresh cream and a gentle', 'lactic finish. Less nutty and complex than aged Gouda', 'but extra rich and silky. Great for melting!'],
  'This is a young Gouda style cheese made with Dutch buffalo milk, aged for about 8 weeks. Because it’s younger, it keeps that soft, elastic texture and super approachable flavor. The high fat content from the buffalo milk gives it that lush, almost melt-in-your-mouth quality without needing long aging. It’s a great intro cheese that still feels special.', array['Honey', 'Apricot jam', 'Green apple', 'Pear', 'Prosciutto', 'Pilsner', 'Light white wines'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'finger-lakes-gold', 'Finger Lakes Gold', 'Lively Run Dairy',
  'Interlaken', 'NY', 'USA',
  'pasteurized Goat’s milk', 'microbial', 'gouda',
  'minimum 90 days', array['Nutty', 'Mellow', 'Salty'],
  'Lively Run Goat Dairy has been in operation since 1983, and in that time the cheesemaking has been passed down from Suzanne Messmer to her son Pete. Finger Lakes Gold is their award-winning gouda style cheese. It won 1st in its category at ACS in 2025', array['malty ales', 'IPA’s', 'Belgian-style beers', 'lagers', 'bourbon', 'Merlot', 'Cabernet Franc', 'Chardonnay'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
