),
(
  'jake-s-aged-gouda', 'Jake’s Aged Gouda', 'Jake’s Gouda Creamery',
  'Deansboro', 'New York', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Gouda',
  '6 months minimum', array['Sweet and brothy', 'nutty', 'approachable', 'intermittent crystallization'],
  'Still handmade in Upstate NY, Jake’s cheese has its roots in Holland. It’s turned daily on pine planks to ensure uniform age and perfection for at least sixty days and it’s covered with a cream coating instead of a wax seal. It’s also a raw milk cheese – no high temp pasteurization here. The results? One of New York’s finest traditional style Gouda cheeses.', array['Fuller bodied reds', 'especially Argentinian Malbec', 'cherry juice', 'cola', 'dried fruit'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'jake-s-baby-gouda', 'Jake’s Baby Gouda', 'Jake’s Gouda Creamery',
  'Deansboro', 'New York', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Gouda (washed curd)',
  '60 days minimum', array['Sweet', 'nutty', 'pliable texture', 'agreeable'],
  'Our Baby Gouda is softer and smoother than it’s aged counterpart. But,just because it’s delicate doesn’t mean it doesn’t have full grown Gouda Goodness. It’s still handmade in Upstate NY, and crafted in the traditional Dutch style. True Gouda needs to breathe and our baby get’s plenty of air. Turned daily on pine planks to ensure uniform age and perfection for at least sixty days, it’s also a raw milk cheese – no high temp pasteurization here. The results? One of New York’s finest traditional style Gouda cheese!', array['Dry Riesling', 'black tea', 'cured meats', 'pickles', 'ginger ale', 'PBR'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'jake-s-smoked-gouda', 'Jake’s Smoked Gouda', 'Jake’s Gouda Creamery',
  'Deansboro', 'New York', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Gouda (washed curd), Smoked',
  '60 day minimum', array['Smokey', 'approachable', 'meltable'],
  'Jake’s personal favorite: Smoked Gouda. This latest addition is flavored after it has aged at least 60 days. Not for the faint of heart, Jake’s Smoked Gouda has a smooth, smoked oak flavor. True Gouda needs to breathe so our cheese gets plenty of air. Turned daily on pine planks to ensure uniform age and perfection for at least sixty days, it’s also a raw milk cheese – no high temp pasteurization here. The results? One of New York’s finest traditional style Smoked Gouda cheeses!', array['Ales', 'floral red wines', 'salami', 'melt on burgers', 'soda'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'natty-gouda', 'Natty Gouda', 'Urban Stead Dairy',
  'Cincinnati', 'Ohio', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Jersey Cow’s milk', 'Animal', 'Dutch style Gouda, natural rind',
  '18-24 months', array['Firm and slightly crystalline with a rich', 'savory-sweet balance. Notes of salted caramel', 'butterscotch', 'and brown butter with a deep', 'lingering umami finish. Subtle grassy undertones come through from the natural rind.'],
  'Made by Urban Stead Dairy in Cincinnati using milk from a third-generation Ohio Valley farm. This is a Dutch-style Gouda aged well past a year, allowing those classic caramelized flavors and protein crystals to develop. The natural rind helps preserve a more rustic, grassy character compared to waxed Goudas. It’s also a super decorated cheese, consistently placing in major competitions like ACS and World Cheese Awards.', array['Apple butter', 'Pear', 'Candied pecans', 'Peanut brittle', 'Dark chocolate', 'Butter crackers', 'Whole grain mustard', 'Riesling', 'Pinot Noir', 'Amber ale', 'Stout', 'Cider'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'old-farmdal', 'Old Farmdal', 'Deweer Family at Kaasboerderij’T Groendal',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'West Flanders', 'Belgium',
  'Pasteurized cow milk', 'vegetarian Rennet', 'Gouda',
  '9 months', array['Dense and slightly fudgy with pronounced tyrosine crystals throughout. Sweet and savory with notes of caramel', 'stone fruit', 'and a subtle “boozy” cherry quality. Finishes with a light acidity reminiscent of dark chocolate.'],
  'Old Farmdal was created by the Deweer family as a younger counterpart to their well-known OG Kristal Gouda. Using the same milk and core process, they adjusted the cultures to develop a similar depth of flavor in less time. It’s aged about half as long but still delivers those crunchy crystals and layered sweetness, making it a great “in-between” Gouda.', array['Dried cherries', 'prosciutto', 'amber ale', 'chocolate covered espresso beans'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'stompetoren-grand-cru', 'Stompetoren Grand Cru', 'CONO',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'North Holland', 'Netherlands',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal', 'Gouda',
  '18 months minimum', array['Complex', 'nutty', 'toffee', 'brothy', 'crystalline'],
  'Stompetoren cheese is made from meadow milk. Our cows graze and rest in the meadow. As a result, they are ''more comfortable in their own skin'' and healthier. Eating fresh grass also ensures a richer, tastier milk. Last year, the cows walked outside for at least 10 hours a day on average 185 days a year. We are happy to reward our farmers with a special premium for this. Stompetoren cheese is made in the CONO cheese factory in North Holland. This cheese factory is regarded as the best & greenest cheese factory in the Netherlands. Our cheese makers still stir the curd by hand and we use the most modern, sustainable techniques to produce as energy-efficiently as possible.', array['Port', 'coffee', 'malbec', 'Dutch Ale', 'drinking chocolate', 'cherries'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'feta-voras', 'Feta Voras', 'Brothers Sokratis and Andreas, exclusively imported by Essex',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Northwestern', 'Greece',
  'Primarily Florina Sheep plus a little goat’s milk', 'Animal', 'Brined',
  '3 months', array['Salty', 'crumbly', 'oceanic'],
  'Feta Voras is produced in the Florina province, located in the far northwestern corner of Greece, near Mount Voras, one of the highest peaks in the region. This area is characterized by its mountainous terrain, wildflowers, and herbs, providing an ideal grazing ground for sheep. The cheese is made by brothers Sokratis and Andreas, who are third-generation cheesemakers, using primarily Florina breed sheep''s milk with a small percentage of goat''s milk, adhering to traditional methods that have been passed down through generations. Florina is one of the seven regions that can make traditional PDO feta. It’s made in small blocks, sprinkled with sea salt from the port of Patras, aged for about three months, then sliced into wedges and packed up for shipment to New York.', array['Used for topping dishes', 'eaten as-is', 'stuffed in olives', 'great with Assyrtiko', 'cheap beer', 'fizzy water', 'watermelon'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'lesbos-feta', 'Lesbos Feta', 'Cheesemaker Pangiotis Tastanis Dairy M&D Tastanis, est. 1980, imported by Essex St. Cheese',
  'Agra', 'Lesbos', 'Greece',
  'Pasteurized Lesbian Sheep', 'Animal', 'Brined',
  '4-18 months', array['custard', 'milk', 'sea salt'],
  'Feta is an ancient cheese. In Homer''s Odyssey, Ulysses found feta in the cave of Polyphemos the Cyclops. Feta is also a much maligned cheese, copied everywhere, made with more care for the bottom line than for flavor. Until recently anyone could call their cheese feta and the country that made the most feta in the world was Germany. Now there are only a few locations that can make the real thing and the island of Lesbos is one of them. Essex feta is made exclusively from the milk of Lesbian breed sheep. The shepherds graze them on the sun-and-sea splashed hills around the village of Agra, on the western side of the island, a tradition that’s been practiced for millenia.', array['Used for topping dishes', 'eaten as-is', 'stuffed in olives', 'great with Assyrtiko', 'cheap beer', 'fizzy water', 'watermelon'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'o-banon', 'O’Banon', 'Capriole Creamery',
  'Greenville', 'Indiana', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Goat', 'Animal Rennet', 'Fresh, Wrapped in chestnut leaves macerated in Bourbon',
  'Wrapped and shipped practically immediately. Shelf life until 180 days after time of wrapping', array['Clean', 'bright', 'vanilla-spice', 'boozy'],
  'Wrapped up like a gift in bourbon-soaked chestnut leaves, O’Banon is all the excuse needed for a celebration. This fresh goat cheese round initially has a bright, tart-fruit flavor balanced by an underlying sweetness and mild tannic note. The paste is dense but softly cloudlike, a testament to Capriole’s hand-ladling process.', array['Bourbon! Chai tea', 'luxardo cherries', 'old fashioned', 'Drambuie'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'sach-paneer', 'Sach Paneer', 'Sach Foods',
  'San Francisco', 'California', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized, organic cow’s milk', 'NA', 'Fresh, acid-coagulated',
  'NA', array['Neutral', 'heatable', 'versatile'],
  'Rooted in Indian cuisine, paneer is a time-tested, nutrient rich food that’s also a high-protein favorite for millions around the world. It’s a fresh cheese that doesn’t melt. Paneer is rich in healthy fats that keep you full longer. Sach’s Original paneer is keto-friendly, gluten-free, and made with sustainably sourced organic milk that come from small humane certified farms. It is soft, crumbly, and melts in your mouth. With a very neutral taste, our original paneer is created for consumers, including kids, to just snack on. In addition to snacking, we also love using our paneer to cook traditional Indian dishes like Saag Paneer or simply sautéing it with some veggies. Our paneer sears fairly quickly and makes for a quick and delicious weeknight meal. It''s also great on the air fryer. **Paneer, like Halloumi, have an ability to stay intact when heated. This melting property (or lack thereof) is attributed to the pH in the milk. For further inquiries regarding the science, please defer to Sarah.', array['Used for cooking. Can be treated like fish and basted and baked with lemon and dill', 'fried', 'slathered in chimichurri and roasted', 'sauteed', 'etc.'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'saltbush-chevre', 'Saltbush Chevre', 'Woodside Cheese Wrights',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Adelaide Hills', 'Australia',
  'Pasteurized Goat', 'NA', 'Acid-coagulated, fresh, rolled in saltbush',
  'NA', array['Clean', 'tangy', 'lactic', 'herbaceous'],
  'Saltbush Goat Chèvre is a stunning fusion of fresh, creamy goat cheese and the unique, herbaceous flavours of native Australian saltbush. This tangy, lightly rolled chèvre is salty and aromatic, making it a perfect addition to your next cheese board. Handmade in the Adelaide Hills using locally sourced goat milk, our goat chèvre is crafted with care and attention to detail. We source our milk from small, family-owned farms, ensuring we maintain complete control over the quality and seasonality of the product. Our herds, including Saanens, British Alpine, and Toggenburg goats, contribute to the rich, smooth texture of the cheese.', array['An herbaceous white wine', 'Riesling from Adelaide Hills', 'herbal tea', 'herbaceous salami', 'stuffed in olives', 'stuffed in dates', 'fresh berries and juice ripe cherries'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'cabot-clothbound-cheddar', 'Cabot Clothbound Cheddar', 'Cabot Creamery/Aged at Jasper Hill',
  'Greensboro', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal Rennet', 'Clothbound Cheddar',
  '9-14 months', array['Complex', 'earthy', 'grassy', 'mustard greens', 'bovine', 'crumbly'],
  'Cabot Clothbound is an approachable but complex natural-rind, bandaged cheddar with a crumbly texture and nutty aroma. The flavor is deeply savory and slightly tangy with caramel sweetness to the finish. In 2003, Cabot Creamery asked us to age a special batch of cheddar, sparking a revolutionary collaboration. After more than a decade the cheese has developed into the cornerstone of our collection. After it comes to the Cellars, we coat the young cheese in lard and add an additional layer of cloth. The cheeses ripen in a specially calibrated vault in our Cellars, where they are constantly brushed, turned, and monitored for quality.', array['California Cabernet Sauvignon', 'Brown Ale', 'Riesling', 'Southern Rhone Grenache', 'chicory', 'mocha latte', 'cured meats', 'olives', 'pickles', 'and other fermented foodstuffs'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'jake-s-3-year-cheddar', 'Jake’s 3 Year Cheddar', 'Jake’s Gouda Creamery',
  'Deansboro', 'New York', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Cheddar',
  '3 Years', array['Sharpish', 'grassy', 'sulfuric', 'meltable'],
  'When Jake and Sylvia began looking searching for their perfect 200-acre farm, their final decision landed them in Deansboro, New York. Deansboro remains a wonderful location for a dairy farm with easy access to feed mills and cattle dealers. The move from Pennsylvania to Upstate New York brought a change of climate. Cooler summers for the cows and perfect conditions for dairy production. Having purchased two farms with intentions of passing them down to their sons, they now have a self-sufficient farm to source their own milk production. Eventually, Jake would like to hand the dairy farm over to his sons, allowing more time for he and Sylvia to pursue their passion for cheesemaking, and the rewarding joy that comes with it.', array['Kolsh', 'Bitter ale', 'Root beer', 'pickles', 'crackers', 'melt in recipes'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'maple-smoked-cheddar', 'Maple Smoked Cheddar', 'Grafton Village Cheese Creamery',
  'Grafton', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Cheddar',
  '12 months', array['Mild', 'campfire', 'slightly sweet', 'meltable'],
  'The Grafton Cooperative Cheese Company was founded in 1892 by dairy farmers who gathered together in a cooperative to make their surplus raw milk into cheese. In the days before refrigeration, there were many such cooperatives in rural agricultural communities and an abundance of fresh, creamy milk was turned into a food that could be stored for a longer period of time. This young cheddar is cold-smoked over maple and hardwood for up to four hours, imparting the signature aroma and satisfying flavor of this classic cheese.', array['Kolsch', 'old world Syrah', 'Porter', 'cured meats', 'dried fruit'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'red-butte-hatch-chile-cheddar', 'Red Butte Hatch Chile Cheddar', 'Bee Hive Cheese',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Utah', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Vegetarian', 'Cheddar, cooked/pressed, hatch chili',
  'About 4 months', array['spicy', 'creamy texture', 'meltable', 'salty'],
  'Red Butte began as a collaboration with Harmons Neighborhood Grocer during Hatch Chile season. The cheese was such a success that Harmons suggested it should be available to everyone. Today, it is our second-best-selling cheese. Named after Red Butte Garden, a botanical garden at the University of Utah in Salt Lake City, this cheese reflects our deep Utah roots. Beehive Cheese has long supported Red Butte Garden, making the name a natural choice to honor our connection to the community. 1st Place World Cheese Awards 2021 1st Place & Best in Show Utah Cheese Awards 2021 3rd Place International Cheese and Dairy Awards 2021', array['simple beer', 'off-dry Riesling', 'meltable–nachos', 'enchiladas', 'cheese dip'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'widmer-s-2-year', 'Widmer’s 2 Year', 'Widmer’s Cheese Cellar',
  'Theresa', 'Wisconsin', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized Cow', 'Animal', 'Cheddar',
  '2 Years', array['Nutty', 'approachable', 'meltable'],
  'In Wisconsin, the cheese making legacy runs deep and examples of third-and fourth generation Wisconsin cheese makers carrying on the family tradition are common. Joe Widmer, of Widmer’s Cheese Cellars in tiny Theresa, Wisconsin, is one such third-generation example. Born into the craft and raised with his six siblings in quarters above the cheese plant, Widmer has succeeded in building the business with a combination of strict adherence to tradition and savvy marketing. Widmer’s best known for producing Brick cheese and traditional stirred-curd Colby, both Wisconsin original created in small towns nearby. More recently, Widmer has gained fame for his four-year cheddar, a 2002 ACS winner and, according to Joe, a specialty that’s fast become a signature product, changing demographics, in a part, are credited with the tipping of the scales in term of sales and production from brick to cheddar.', array['Ales', 'Boxed Wine', 'Dr. Pepper', 'melt in recipes', 'good for cheese sauce on broccoli'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'ba-ba-blue', 'Ba Ba Blue', 'Carr Valley',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Central Wisconsin', 'USA',
  'Raw or Pasteurized Sheep', 'Animal', 'Blue',
  '4 months', array['Rich', 'milky', 'mild', 'slightly peppery', 'and gets more intense with age'],
  'Owned and operated by the Cook family, Carr Valley Cheese Company is over one-hundred years old. Nestled amongst the rolling hills and lush pastures of central Wisconsin, we remain one of Wisconsin''s traditional cheese plants, famous for making cheese the old-fashioned way! Milk is sourced from local farms.', array['walnuts', 'whole muscle charcuterie', 'coffee', 'Sauternes', 'Merlot'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
