(
  'rogue-river-blue', 'Rogue River Blue', 'Rogue Creamery',
  'Rogue River Valley', 'Southern Oregon', 'USA',
  'Pasteurized, organic cow', 'Vegetarian', 'Blue, Wrapped in Syrah grape leaves that have been macerated in pear spirit',
  '9-12 months', array['Boozy', 'piquant', 'complex'],
  'As fall comes to the Rogue Valley, cooler temperatures and wet weather bring renewed growth to the pastures. This is when our cow’s milk is at its best – and it’s only during these months that we make our limited edition, seasonal Rogue River Blue – a cheese named World Champion at the 2019/20 World Cheese Awards. After 9 to 11 months of careful tending in our aging caves, our team hand-wraps each wheel in organic, biodynamic Syrah grape leaves that have soaked in pear spirits. On the Autumnal Equinox each year, we celebrate the release of the year’s new Rogue River Blue Cheese.', array['Pear Brandy', 'poached pears', 'apple juice', 'walnuts and honey'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'shakerag-blue', 'Shakerag Blue', 'Sequatchie Cove',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Tennessee', 'USA',
  'pasteurized cow', 'animal rennet', 'Flavored Blue',
  '4 months', array['rich and creamy balanced with the sharpness of the blue veining', 'some say it reminds them of Juicy Fruit gum'],
  'The soaking of the fig leaves in local whiskey before vacuum sealing for aging is a nod to the cheese’s namesake. According to legend, a thirsty person could leave a white rag and coins in a tree stump. When they returned later, a jar of moonshine would be waiting. The family creamery owned by Nathan and Padgett Arnold is 100% solar powered with grass fed Jersey and Jersey-Holstein cows', array['Chattanooga Whiskey', 'root beer', 'dried fruit and nuts or melted on top of a steak or crumbled in a salad'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'stilton-pdo', 'Stilton PDO', 'Colston Bassett',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Nottinghamshire', 'United Kingdom',
  'pasteurized Cow', 'Traditional', 'blue veined',
  '3 - 4 months', array['Fudgy', 'Salted Graham Crackers', 'Sweet Cream'],
  'Stilton is an EU protected food name, meaning it can only be produced in the English counties of Derbyshire, Nottinghamshire, and Leicestershire where it’s said to have originated. Stilton must be made with pasteurized milk by law, this is what differentiates Stilton & Stichelton! Colston Bassett is a top tier Stilton with only four cheesemakers in the last one hundred years. Colston Bassett has maintained a tradition and quality of cheesemaking that is unparalleled in the Stilton world. All the milk for this Stilton comes from within 1.5 miles of the dairy', array['Port wine', 'Graham Crackers', 'Chocolate cookies', 'stouts & porters'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'stichelton', 'Stichelton', 'Stichelton Dairy',
  'Welbeck Estate in Nottinghamshire', '.', 'United Kingdom',
  'Raw cow (Andersonville Herd)', 'traditional', 'blue veined',
  '4–8 months', array['sweet cream', 'apple cider', 'herbs', 'savory finish'],
  'Withersbrook Blue is made from raw milk from Jasper Hill Farm’s Andersonville herd in Greensboro, Vermont. After an initial aging period in the Cellars at Jasper Hill, the cheese develops delicate blue veining and a dense, creamy paste. The cheese is then soaked with Eden Ice Cider, a dessert cider produced by leaving apple cider outdoors through the Vermont winter. Freezing concentrates the sugars while removing excess water, resulting in a cider with bright acidity and intense apple character. This soaking process gently infuses the cheese, adding fruit and acidity without overwhelming the blue. The result is a cheese that feels balanced and layered, moving from sweet cream and apple to a lingering savory finish. Customer Type: Blue curious customers, cider lovers, dessert cheese fans, sweet savory palates. How to sell it in one sentence: “A creamy raw milk blue soaked in Vermont ice cider with apple sweetness and gentle funk.”', array['Ice cider', 'ribeye', 'honey', 'lemon curd'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'alfred-le-fermier', 'Alfred Le Fermier', 'Fromagerie La Station',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Quebec', 'Canada',
  'organic raw cows milk (Holstein)', 'animal', 'semi-hard',
  '8-24 months', array['nutty', 'fruity', 'savory and herbaceous with hint of caramel and roasted hazelnuts'],
  'Fourth generation farmers following in the footsteps of Alfred Boldec, their ancestor who has been farming the land since 1928. They prioritize the health and well being of their 150 Holstein herd and the quality of the cheese they produce. Cheese is aged on wooden boards. Named First Place Best of Show at 2025 American Cheese Society Judging and Competition.', array['honey and fresh apples with rustic', 'shiraz'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'alp-blossom', 'Alp Blossom', 'Hofkäserei Kraus / Maker to Monger Imports it',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Bavaria', 'Germany',
  'raw, cow', 'traditional', 'alpine, cooked pressed',
  '7 months', array['Savory', 'Herbaceous', 'Cooked Cashews', 'Oregano', '(honestly tastes like Pizza Combos)'],
  'Paying tribute to the Alpine environment that helps shape and flavor the milk used in production, this cheese is coated in a diverse combination of dried flower petals, herbs, and spices that grow out in the pastures surrounding the dairy. The cheese is literally coated in the same things that the cows are grazing on. Head cheesemaker Albert Kraus sources milk from his brother’s neighboring herd of Brown Swiss cows. Brown Swiss cattle are known for the high butterfat content of their milk, which yields a cheese with a golden inner paste and a creamy toothsome bite.', array['Dry Reisling', 'hefeweizen', 'jasmine tea', 'clover honey', 'dark chocolate', 'olive oil', 'bresaola'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'alpha-tolman', 'Alpha Tolman', 'Jasper Hill Farm',
  'Greensboro', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Alpine, cooked/pressed',
  '8-12 months', array['Meaty', 'bone broth', 'allium', 'meltable'],
  'ALPHA TOLMAN is named for a philanthropic dairy farmer who built the Greensboro library in 1900. Alpha''s grandfather, Enoch, was one of our town''s original settlers. His namesake cheese is made at our renovated Jasper Hill Creamery in Greensboro, Vermont. Alpha Tolman is now being made with our “Sax Rennet”—a traditional rennet made using cultures from previous makes and calf vells.', array['Ale', 'Porter', 'Red Burgundy', 'Cider', 'Apple Juice', 'Iced Mocha', 'pickles', 'apricot jam', 'prosciutto'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'ashbrook', 'Ashbrook', 'Spring Brook Farm',
  'Reading', 'VT', 'USA',
  'Raw Jersey Cow', 'Animal', 'Washed rind/Morbier-Style',
  '~3 Months', array['Savory and earthy with aromas of damp cellar', 'cultured butter', 'mushrooms', 'and mild funk. The paste is sweet and milky with a subtle vegetal tang from the line of vegetable ash running through the center.'],
  'Made at Spring Brook Farm in Vermont, Ashbrook is the farm’s New England-inspired take on Morbier. Crafted with raw Jersey cow milk and aged for about three months, the cheese features a distinctive line of vegetable ash through the paste in homage to the traditional French style. Spring Brook Farm operates alongside Farms for City Kids, an educational nonprofit focused on connecting urban youth with agriculture, making the creamery deeply tied to both land and community.', array['green apple', 'prosciutto', 'Riesling', 'hoppy ale'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'cyclamen-comte', 'Cyclamen Comte', 'Marcel Petit',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Fort St Antoine', 'France',
  'raw cow', 'traditional', 'alpine, cooked-pressed',
  '30 months', array['rich', 'roasted pork', 'cooked nuts', 'crystalline'],
  'The name “Cyclamen” is a reference to a type of Millesime that is particularly prized for its quality and long aging. Millésime is a French term translating to "vintage" or a "great vintage," typically referring to the specific year a wine or Champagne was produced. Marcel Petit ages all of the comtes in the side of a Mountain in the Jura range. The aging cellars are what was once Fort St Antoine, a military fortress. It keeps the temperature lower and the humidity up allowing the older age profiles to have a softness about them still while developing a robust flavor profile', array['vin de jura', 'Poulsard', 'amber ale', 'toasted walnuts', 'dry ciders', 'apricots'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'fontina-valle-d-aosta', 'Fontina Valle D’Aosta', 'Two Cooperatives via Forever Cheese',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Valle D’Aosta', 'Italy',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Cooked/unpressed, washed rind, alpine',
  '3 months', array['Fruity', 'herbaceous', 'floral', 'nutty', 'meltable'],
  'The original Fontina produced in the Italian Alps is a semisoft, washed-rind unpasteurized cow’s milk cheese aged about 3 months. Rich and buttery, Fontina finishes with an earthy flavor. It’s excellent for fondues and au gratin dishes. The single-farm Alpeggio version is made exclusively with the summer milk of Valdostana cows grazing on Alpine pastures (1900+m). We’ve hand-selected our two favorite dairies to bring you this special cheese, available only 3 months of the year (November-February).', array['Wines of the region', 'herbaceous Vermentino', 'brandy', 'grappa', 'olives', 'cured meats'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'gruyere-surchoix-surchoix-means-first-choice-or-top-quality', 'Gruyere Surchoix (‘Surchoix’ means first choice, or top quality)', 'Gourmino',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Gruyere', 'Switzerland',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Alpine, Cooked/pressed, Smear-ripened',
  '12 months', array['Complex', 'fruity', 'floral', 'herbaceous', 'meaty', 'nutty', 'etc. Meltable.'],
  'Le Gruyère AOP, the unique cheese from the French-speaking part of Switzerland, tastes of delicate mountain flowers and wonderful alpine herbs that are typical for the region. Its history goes back to the year 1115: Already then, the milk from the picturesque villages of the Gruyère region was processed by the local cheesemakers into a remarkable product with a strong character. Won Best in Show at the World Cheese Awards in 2022', array['Chasselas', 'German Pinot Noir', 'Dry Riesling', 'German-style ales', 'Kirsch', 'Black cherry soda', 'plowman’s board fare', 'brasaola', 'grapes', 'pears and apples', 'Quince'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'hornbacher', 'Hornbacher', 'Michael Spycher',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Wasen', 'Switzerland',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Alpine, cooked/pressed',
  '12 months', array['Baked potato', 'scallions', 'roasted nuts', 'burnt sugar', 'umami'],
  'Michu, as Michael Spycher is called by his friends, has been producing the Hornbacher for 25 years. The cheese got its name from the small river that flows through right next to the dairy. Until 2014 Michu and his wife Monika sold the specialty only in their cheese shop. With growing popularity, the two decide to produce more of the Hornbacher to meet local and export market demands.', array['Malty brew', 'Herbal red wines', 'Root beer', 'Drip coffee', 'pickled onions', 'tart jam', 'onion jam', 'olives', 'cured', 'fatty meats'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'le-cousin', 'Le Cousin', 'Schmidthauser (family-run)',
  'Made in Thurgau', '; aged in Haute-Savoie', 'France',
  'Raw Cow’s Milk', 'Animal Rennet', 'Cooked, pressed semi-hard (Alpine-style, smear-rind)',
  '6 Months', array['Toasted butter', 'nutty', 'and gently fruity with a sweet-salty tang. Hints of pasture', 'grass', 'and hay. Mildly funky for a smear rind', 'with a creamy', 'semi-firm paste that has a little give.'],
  'A true border-crossing alpine cheese. Le Cousin is made in Switzerland by a member of the Schmidthauser family, then transported to France where another branch of the family ages it in their cellars in Haute-Savoie. That Swiss-French handoff is the whole identity of the cheese. It sits on the milder side of the alpine smear-rind spectrum, closer to Gruyère and Comté than anything aggressively funky. The rind develops a beautiful pink-orange hue and is absolutely worth eating.', array['white wine', 'light red', 'cornichons', 'crusty bread', 'caramelized onions'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'l-etivaz', 'L’Etivaz', 'L’Etivaz Cooperative–Gourmino',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Vaud Alps', 'Switzerland',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Alpine',
  '15-24 months', array['Alliums', 'toasted nuts', 'purple flowers', 'broth', 'and much more'],
  'L’Etivaz AOP is a hard Alpine cheese made by hand from 10 May to 10 October, with raw milk, fresh from the farm. 3,000 cows graze in about 130 Alpine pastures located at altitudes of 1,000 to 2,000 metres, supplying each day rich, floral milk that is heated exclusively over wood fires in copper cauldrons. The ripening process brings out the rich, powerful aromas that come from the wide variety of grasses eaten by the cows. The Rosat family tends to 45 cows during the summer on the Antheines Alp. They rotate productions between 3 huts at different altitudes. When the temperatures are still cool in spring or autumn and the upper alpine meadows are still snow-covered, the cows live on the two lower-lying Alps. This allows the cows to eat fresh grass throughout the summer and to enjoy the rich alpine flora. After the curds are cut, they are heated exclusively in copper kettles over a wood fire. Due to the long maturing process, the intense, strong aromas of the alpine herbs eaten by the cows unfold perfectly in the cheese. Every year in autumn, Gourmino visits the cellars of the L’Etivaz AOP Cooperative to taste the cheeses from last summer. We select the best cheeses for our customers, paying attention to a typical, balanced taste profile and consistency in quality. The selected cheeses are then taken to the cellars of the Gourmino, where they are ready for delivery.', array['Herbaceous wines', 'suds', 'root beer', 'cured meats', 'use for fondue', 'dried cherries', 'pears'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'mountaineer', 'Mountaineer', 'Meadow Creek Dairy',
  'Galax', 'VA', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow’s Milk', 'Animal Rennet', 'Alpine style; Washed Rind',
  '6-9 Months', array['Roasted nuts', 'toasted bread', 'beef broth', 'caramel', 'browned butter', 'subtle citrus', 'savory alpine funk. Texture is semi-hard', 'supple', '‘melt in your mouth’'],
  'Made high in Virginia’s Blue Ridge Mountains from Meadow Creek’s own Jersey herd, Mountaineer is an Appalachian take on classic alpine cheeses like Comté and Raclette. Aged for at least six months, it develops a rich, savory depth with a supple, melt-in-the-mouth texture. Though it falls into the washed rind family, the funk stays balanced by buttery sweetness, roasted nuts, and a warm brothy finish. Mountaineer melts beautifully like Raclette while carrying the deeper caramelized complexity of longer-aged alpine cheeses. Its aroma opens with toasted bread and parmesan-like notes before becoming more floral and fruity as it warms.', array['Fruit lambic', 'sour cherry preserves', 'saison', 'caramelized onions', 'dry cider'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'pleasant-ridge-reserve', 'Pleasant Ridge Reserve', 'Uplands Cheese',
  'Dodgeville', 'Wisconsin', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Alpine-style, cooked/pressed, smear-ripened',
  'Each batch develops at their own pace, but PRR is aged less than a year. Extra aged version is aged for a year plus.', array['Complex', 'pastoral', 'nutty', 'floral–varies from batch to batch'],
  'Pleasant Ridge is the most-awarded cheese in American history, having won Best of Show in the American Cheese Society’s annual competition three times (2001, 2005 and 2010), and having also won the US Cheese Championships in 2003. It is the only cheese to have won ACS Best of Show three times, and the only cheese to have ever won both of the major, national cheese competitions. Named after the land formation on which our farm sits, Pleasant Ridge Reserve is made in the tradition of Alpine cheeses like Gruyere and Beaufort. Like the Alpage versions of these cheeses, we only make Pleasant Ridge Reserve from May through October when our cows are eating fresh pasture. This grass-fed, raw milk produces flavors in the cheese that can’t be replicated by “ordinary” milk. In mid-summer, when the cows are at the peak of their production, a batch of cheese may yield up to 78, 10-lb wheels a day. Because we’re very particular about using milk from only the best pasture conditions, the weather largely determines how many batches we can make in a year. When the pasture conditions aren’t ideal, we sell the milk. Some years we’re able to make more cheese than other years. This may seem like a luxury, but using only the ideal milk is the most important way we ensure the quality of our cheese.', array['Cherry jam', 'Effie’s Cocoa Cakes', 'Cider', 'Sour Ale', 'capers'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'raclette-livradois-pronounced-leev-wa-dwa', 'Raclette Livradois (pronounced leev-wa-dwa)', 'Livradois',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Savoie', 'France',
  'Thermized Cow', 'Microbial', 'Raclette, washed rind, uncooked/pressed',
  '5 months', array['Clean', 'fruity', 'alliums', 'meltable'],
  'Livradois is an independant family business since 3 generations. Product made from local cow’s milk in the middle of the regional natural park of Livradois. Soft and melting paste with fruity taste. One of the last producers to offer unpasteurized Raclette Known as principal ingredient at the time of the Raclette', array['Kirsch', 'cherry juice', 'lingonberry jam', 'Dr. Pepper', 'ham', 'pickles', 'olives', 'mustard', 'potatoes', 'bread. Great al fresco on a plowman’s board.'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'raclette-livradois-with-ramps', 'Raclette Livradois with Ramps', 'Livradois',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Savoie', 'France',
  'Thermized cow', 'Microbial', 'Alpine, washed rind, uncooked, pressed',
  '5 months', array['Alliums', 'umami', 'meltable', 'amicable'],
  'Livradois is an independant family business since 3 generations. Product made from local cow’s milk in the middle of the regional natural park of Livradois. Soft and melting paste with fruity taste. One of the last producers to offer unpasteurized Raclette Known as principal ingredient at the time of the Raclette', array['Raclette accoutrement', 'blonde ale', 'gose', 'cola', 'herbal tea'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
