),
(
  'raclette-de-savoie', 'Raclette de Savoie', 'Schmidhauser',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Savoie/Haute Savoie', 'France',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Washed Rind, Uncooked, pressed',
  '3 months minimum', array['Fruity', 'complex', 'toasted hazelnuts', 'savory', 'and more. Highly meltable.'],
  'With a generational family history in affinage starting in Switzerland (the German speaking part, obvi), Schmidhauser sources high quality milk from small farms and utilizes traditional practices.', array['Kirsch', 'cherry juice', 'pomegranate arils', 'raclette accoutrement'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'rahmtaler-reserve', 'Rahmtaler Reserve', 'exclusively made by Gourmino',
  'Not provided by creamery', 'Langnau', 'Switzerland',
  'full fat, raw cow’s milk', 'traditional', 'cooked pressed, alpine',
  '10+ months', array['Cashews', 'Cooked Milk', 'Plantains', 'Citrus Fruits'],
  'Rahmtaler is basically actually the original Emmentaler. The original recipe for Emmentaler, from the 16th century, called for full fat milk. In the 20th century it fell off and became produced with skimmed milk. In 2016 Gourmino bought the exclusive rights to the original recipe and became the only ones available to produce this original, which they now call Rahmtaler. The reserve wheels are hand-selected and brought to the caves at Reichenbach to mature fully', array['sourdough bread for a grilled cheese', 'all beef hot dogs', 'Chardonnay', 'Champagne', 'Chasselass', 'dijon mustard', 'sauerkraut', 'rye bread', 'hazelnuts'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'rupert', 'Rupert', 'Woodlawn Creamery ( but was previously made by Consider Bardwell which closed, Woodlawn supplied all the milk for this cheese so it was a natural transition)',
  'Pawlet', 'VT', 'USA',
  'raw, cow', 'traditional', 'alpine style',
  '6 - 12 months', array['Fruity', 'Butterscotch', 'Yeasty'],
  'A young alpine-style cheese with a butterscotch, yeasted biscuit flavor profile. Woodlawn Creamery has always been a part of Rupert’s story. Following Consider Bardwell’s 2024 closure, seventh generation dairy farmer Seth Leach, and his wife Kate, along with veteran cheesemaker Leslie Goff Tyminski (who had been the cheesemaker at Consider Bardwell until 2019), are making updated versions of Consider Bardwell''s legendary cheeses. Rupert is named for one of the oldest towns in Vermont. I always say this cheese was brought back from near extinction!', array['perfect for melting', 'great mac and cheese base! It’s also a great pairing for bourbon drinks', 'dried cherries', 'cornichons'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'silver-lake', 'Silver Lake', 'East Hill Creamery',
  'Perry', 'NY', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow’s Milk, Grassfed', 'Animal Rennet', 'alpine style, cook pressed',
  'Minimum 1 year', array['Sweet', 'nutty', 'and savory with a deep umami finish. Firm texture with a smooth', 'slightly dense paste. Think toasted nuts', 'browned butter', 'and that classic French onion soup vibe.'],
  'A New York take on classic Alpine cheeses like Comté and Gruyère. Made in large-format wheels and aged on wood boards for at least a year, this cheese leans into that sweet-savory balance with a big umami punch. It’s a local favorite for a reason and consistently wins awards at the New York State Fair.', array['Sauvignon Blanc', 'sour cherry', 'roasted potatoes'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'almn-s-tegel', 'Almnäs Tegel', 'Almnäs Bruk',
  '', '', 'Sweden',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Cooked/pressed, Smear-ripened, Scalded Curds!',
  '16-22 months', array['Roasty-toasty', 'peanutty', 'clean', 'approachable', 'substantial chew'],
  'Almnäs Brick (Almnäs Tegel) is a hard-pressed “scalded” cheese, its square shape inspired by the handmade bricks manufactured by the Almnäs brick factory from the 1750’s onwards. On the rind, you can see the imprint of a small child’s foot, a historical reference to real footprints found in the brick floor in the attic of the manor house. Hundreds of years ago as the bricks dried in the sun, the farm workers’ children ran over them, leaving their footprints. Since then, a child’s footprint has been imprinted on every clay brick manufactured at Almnas. Brick production ended in 1976, but we continue the tradition today: the same logo is imprinted in the rind of every Almnäs Brick cheese. Each cheese weighs between 20 and 23 kilograms (57 and 59 pounds) and measures 52 x 45 centimeters (20 by 18 inches). The rind is a rustic, brick red, achieved by washing the cheese in salt water. This process benefits a bacterial culture called Brevibacterium linens, which provides the reddish colour. The cut surface of the cheese is smooth, showing occasional small holes and cracks. The cheese colour ranges from ivory to straw, depending on the season. Almnäs Brick has a sweet, fruity aroma, reminiscent of butterscotch. The rind sometimes smells of orange or pineapple. The taste is fruity, with a slightly granular mouth-feel. We store the Almnäs Brick between 16 and 22 months. Scalded cheeses are unusual in traditional Swedish cheese making. At the end of the cheese-making process, we scald the curds by increasing the temperature to more than 50 degrees Celsius (122 degrees Fahrenheit). This gives the cheese a caramelized effect and promotes the Thermophile bacteria, which is also found in yogurt. Parmesan and many of the big cheeses from the Swiss Alps, such as Gruyere, are produced according to this method. At The World Cheese Awards 2018 held in Bergen, Norway, there were 3472 cheeses from 41 countries ans Almnäs Tegel ended up at 4:th place and recived a Supergold. World Cheese Awards 2019, the judges gave Almnäs Tegel a Gold. Held at Bergamo, Italy.', array['Malty beer', 'Red Burgundy', 'Ale (in a tankard)', 'Mead', 'Birch Beer', 'dried fruit'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  't-te-de-moine', 'Tête de Moine', 'AOP-regulated (multiple producers; specific dairy ID varies by wheel)',
  'Bellelay', 'Jura Mountains', 'Switzerland',
  'Raw Cow’s Milk', 'Animal Rennet', 'washed rind, semi-hard alpine',
  '~2-6 Months', array['Buttery', 'nutty', 'and fruity with a savory', 'brothy depth. Notes of caramelized onion', 'light tang', 'and a mild washed rind funk. Aroma opens up big when shaved.'],
  'This is “monk’s head” cheese, originally made by monks at the Abbey of Bellelay over 800 years ago. Instead of cutting it into wedges, you shave it on a girolle into little ruffled rosettes. That shaving isn’t just for looks, it actually releases more aroma and makes the texture feel softer and almost melt-in-your-mouth. The rind is washed in brine, giving it that sticky orange exterior and gentle funk. Historically, wheels were even used as currency.', array['fruit', 'Hoppy Ale', 'cured beef', 'beautiful on a board or cake'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'underpass', 'Underpass', 'East Hill Creamery',
  'Perry', 'NY', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow’s Milk', 'Animal Rennet', 'raclette style; Alpine Style',
  '3 Months', array['Creamy', 'earthy', 'savory', 'and melty with balanced salinity. Sweet alpine notes with a buttery finish and a little tang. The Reserve version develops bolder earthiness with hints of citrus and pineapple on the finish.'],
  'Underpass was East Hill Creamery’s first cheese, named after the underpass they built beneath Route 20A to connect their cow pastures. Inspired by classic Alpine raclette styles, it was designed to melt beautifully while still holding onto that sweet-savory depth. It’s approachable, super versatile, and the kind of cheese that somehow works with nearly everything you throw at it. The Reserve version spends significantly longer in the cave, creating a firmer texture and deeper, more rustic flavor.', array['fresh figs', 'sundried tomatoes', 'sparkling rosé', 'fruity beers'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
),
(
  'whitney', 'Whitney', 'Jasper Hill Farm',
  'Greensboro', 'Vermont', 'USA',
  'Raw Cow', 'Animal', 'Raclette, cooked/unpressed',
  '3-6 months', array['Sour cream', 'toasted nuts', 'cured ham'],
  'WHITNEY - Named after Tim Whitney—Jasper Hill’s longest-standing Team Member—this cheese honors the people behind a mission to set the gold standard of artisan cheese quality. A reflection of community, Whitney is made in a semi-firm mountain style with traditional methods that capture a true “Taste of Place.”', array['Meltable. Dried figs', 'lager', 'Kirsch', 'Cola', 'bresaola'],
  'published', '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2',
  '296fb853-d174-46c7-8e94-e19b1ce61fd2'
)
